{
  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** Readings older than the retention period stop being kept. `src/tide_cache.py` gains a module-level `RETENTION_DAYS` constant, named in the style of `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`), set to the period answered in the section below. `store` (`src/tide_cache.py:4-5`) records when each reading was stored and removes every held reading older than `RETENTION_DAYS` on each call. Age is measured from store time because `store` treats a reading as opaque, and expiry happens in `store` because it is the module's only function (`src/tide_cache.py:1-5`). Nothing else in `src/` imports the module, so the shape of `READINGS` entries can change freely.\n\n**Test contract:** Write these failing tests first, as `unittest.TestCase` methods in `tests/test_tide_cache.py`, following the test layout agreed in [[task/expiry-notice-name-the-reading-in-the-notice-dependent]], with the clock patched and `READINGS` cleared between tests:\n\n- A reading stored less than `RETENTION_DAYS` ago is still held after a later `store`.\n- A reading stored exactly `RETENTION_DAYS` ago is still held after a later `store`: readings expire after the period, not at it.\n- A reading stored more than `RETENTION_DAYS` ago is gone after a later `store`, and the newly stored reading is held.\n\nVerify from the repository root with `python3 -m unittest tests.test_tide_cache`: the tests fail before the change and pass after it.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py` (modified), `tests/test_tide_cache.py` (created)\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `store` keeps every reading with no expiry (`src/tide_cache.py:4-5`). The README states no period (`README.md:1-3`), and nothing in `src/` mentions retention. The vault has no area profile or ADR for this surface. [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]] and [[task/fixture-tide-expiry-spec-the-slice]], the task's related records, state no period. [[task/tide-cache-expire-stale-readings-leftover-answer]] carries an answer of 7 days, but that answer belongs to that record's own escalation, so it is not applied here.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, kept from the earlier draft of this section as a common retention for operational readings. It is a default rather than a derived fact, and nothing in the repository or vault supports it, so the harbour's own policy should replace it if one exists.\n**Answer:** Keep readings for 30 days.\n",
